This directory describes a modified PostgreSQL libpq 18.6 dependency.
The official PostgreSQL source archive and SHA-256 provenance are pinned in source.json.
COPYRIGHT is copied verbatim from that verified source archive.

0001-silent-passfile-rejection.patch removes two passwordFromFile stderr diagnostics
that expose passfile paths before a connection notice callback can be installed.
It preserves file opening, fstat, rejection, cleanup, and configuration precedence.
The adjacent comment is corrected to describe silent rejection.

0002-rpgmigrate-capability.patch adds PQrpgmigrateCapabilities(void), an unsigned-int
constant function returning 1U, its public declaration, and export ordinal 211.
Bit 0 identifies the reviewed silent passfile rejection behavior.
PQlibVersion and the PostgreSQL version remain unchanged.

The build uses installed OpenSSL, Kerberos/GSSAPI, and libcurl dependencies.
Their versions, compiler flags, and local artifact hashes are recorded in
target/native/libpq/artifact.json.
Those external dependencies retain their own licenses and notices.
This build does not copy their libraries or change their installations.

Retain this notice and COPYRIGHT with copies of the modified libpq artifact.
